saturday morning the las vegas strip  will be filled with bikes it's a  memorial ride to honor a tragedy that  happened one year ago tomorrow in fact  marks one year since five cyclists were  killed by an impaired driver near  searchlight bianca holman live this  morning on las vegas boulevard with a  look ahead to this event bianca good  morning  good morning so cyclists and loved ones  of those five cyclists that were killed  want you to grab your bike and join them  out here on the las vegas boulevard they  want to use the event on saturday to  help educate people on what we all can  do to help prevent another deadly crash  of whether it's cyclists pedestrians or  even drivers so you may remember that it  was last december in 2020 a large group  of cyclists were riding near searchlight  with an escort vehicle an impaired truck  driver struck and killed five of those  cyclists it was a horrific event for the  cyclist community loved ones created a  ghost bike memorial right next to a  popular bike path an intersection near  charleston boulevard in the 215. this  year they want to continue to keep their  memory alive and raise awareness to both  drivers and cyclists  we've had senators and congressmen and  commissioners reach out asking even the  state what can we do how can we help and  they seem to be really paying attention  at this point and you know we've had  some safety initiatives with some of our  partners that have been very successful  so yeah we do feel we're making progress  so again the key is to educate folks  this saturday and also share the stories  of the lives of those five cyclists  being michael murray aaron ray  gerald knee deja  tom trogger and auxoy ahmed so those are  those five cyclists that were killed so  their families and friends will all be  out here on saturday we've got the  information on our screen right now so  it's saturday it starts at 6 45 they're  going to be gathering at the church that  is right behind the route 91 memorial  site  and they want to of course bring your  bike helmet and snacks if need be and  that ride is going to start at seven and  then of course there will be a police  escort we have all those details on our  website eight news now dot com bianca  holman live local now
 

